# Generated inventory of the machine this was last run on.
#
# `./capture.sh` writes these. They are genuinely useful — they are what tells a
# rebuild which packages, repos, and databases existed — but they enumerate real
# hostnames, repository URLs, database names, and open ports for whoever ran it.
# That belongs in your own private notes, not in a public repository.
#
# See manifests/README.md, which IS tracked and explains the format.
manifests/*
!manifests/README.md

# Captured Claude Code configuration: your own slash commands, skills, and
# settings. `capture.sh --payload` writes these. They are yours and are almost
# always project- or employer-specific.
files/claude/*
!files/claude/.gitkeep

# Local backup config — contains destination paths, and possibly a bucket name.
laptop-backup.conf

# Editor and OS noise
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
